From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libc: minimal: memcpy: copy words when alignments differ

memcpy copied word by word only when source and destination shared
their alignment, and byte by byte otherwise. For buffers in uncached
memory every byte is then a full bus transaction: a 1472-byte UDP
payload starts 2 bytes off a word boundary in its frame, so the socket
copy into a word-aligned buffer read uncached DDR a byte at a time.

When the alignments differ, align the destination and build each
destination word from two aligned source words, shifted and merged.
Every access is word-sized. The loads stay inside the aligned words
that hold the first and last source bytes, so they cannot cross into
another page or memory protection region.

On a VexRiscv and a MicroBlaze V at 100 MHz with uncached frame
buffers this doubles UDP socket receive, from 9.1 to 18.6 and 19.3
Mbit/s (1472-byte payloads, 100 Mbit/s link).

Signed-off-by: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
---
 lib/libc/minimal/source/string/string.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/libc/minimal/source/string/string.c b/lib/libc/minimal/source/string/string.c
index c801ef31e39..803bfd44eb7 100644
--- a/lib/libc/minimal/source/string/string.c
+++ b/lib/libc/minimal/source/string/string.c
@@ -324,6 +324,42 @@ void *memcpy(void *ZRESTRICT d, const void *ZRESTRICT s, size_t n)
 
 		d_byte = (unsigned char *)d_word;
 		s_byte = (unsigned char *)s_word;
+	} else if (n >= 4 * sizeof(mem_word_t)) {
+
+		/*
+		 * Different alignment: align the destination, then build each
+		 * destination word from two aligned source words. This keeps
+		 * every access word-sized, which matters most when one side is
+		 * uncached memory. The loads never leave the aligned words that
+		 * hold the first and last source bytes.
+		 */
+
+		while (((uintptr_t)d_byte) & mask) {
+			*(d_byte++) = *(s_byte++);
+			n--;
+		}
+
+		const uintptr_t off = (uintptr_t)s_byte & mask;
+		const unsigned int lo = off * 8U;
+		const unsigned int hi = (sizeof(mem_word_t) - off) * 8U;
+		mem_word_t *d_word = (mem_word_t *)d_byte;
+		const mem_word_t *s_word = (const mem_word_t *)(s_byte - off);
+		mem_word_t cur = *(s_word++);
+
+		while (n >= sizeof(mem_word_t)) {
+			mem_word_t next = *(s_word++);
+
+#if __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+			*(d_word++) = (cur << lo) | (next >> hi);
+#else
+			*(d_word++) = (cur >> lo) | (next << hi);
+#endif
+			cur = next;
+			n -= sizeof(mem_word_t);
+		}
+
+		d_byte = (unsigned char *)d_word;
+		s_byte = (const unsigned char *)(s_word - 1) + off;
 	}
 #endif
 
